  "observedBehavior": "Native Task View keyboard/pointer local browsing and actual group/active-marker controls paint. Escape closes the popup without a window-effect request, preserves workspace membership, and returns native incarnation 2 and GTK key a to the surviving opener. When that opener is really destroyed, current presentation acknowledgement precedes one Escape; the popup closes, retired incarnation 2 stays absent/unfocused, no window effect is sent and surviving peer workspace/output stay unchanged.",
  "productionChange": "Capture the exact previous native focused window before grab-end pointer refocus; use it only when current focus is empty, the popup belongs to a keyboard-none layer, and that object is still mapped on a visible workspace. Existing native focus/lock/nofocus policy remains in force.",
  "buildBoundary": "One SeatManager TU compiled/relinked against identical owning public headers; 432 ordered archive payloads preserved, public exports equal. Authority recompiled against the owning identical-header tuple with strict strong-symbol closure. Frozen runtime assets retained; a recorded private host copy changes only the core-selector tuple location.",
  "retiredAttempt": "An extra keyboard-grab reentry patch did not fix the negative observation and is retired. Protocol/GDK trace shows Escape arrived before presentation-applied for the replacement frame. The final negative fixture waits the real current-frame acknowledgement under the unchanged six-second observation deadline; it does not move focus or repeat Escape.",
